@copilot Update this PR directly to remove the separate Java 17 Quarkus smoke-image pin. The maintainer wants the same rollout as #12541 and #12567: build and publish the new images first, then switch the one shared test tag and drop the JDK that the new Quarkus version no longer supports.

For this PR, delete `QUARKUS_JAVA_17_VERSION` and remove the ternary in `QuarkusSmokeTest`, so it uses `QUARKUS_VERSION` for all image tags as before. Remove the temporary rollout comment from `TestImageVersions`; the PR description will cover the rollout. Keep the current published `QUARKUS_VERSION` value and the Java 17, 21, 25, and 27 test cases unchanged for now. In a separate change after the normal Quarkus 4 image publishing workflow has run, the maintainer will update the shared tag and drop Java 17 together. Do not publish images, merge, or open a separate PR. Keep the Quarkus 4 build changes and the workflow's Java 17 skip intact, and do not touch the agent's Java support or the separate Quarkus 3 instrumentation tests.

Limit this cleanup to the two smoke test source files. Follow the repository's Gradle instructions, apply the narrow formatter, and run the targeted `QuarkusSmokeTest` if Docker is available. Report what actually ran and any limitations.

